# WeiDU mod / component identity

Full narrative: [docs/weidu-install.md](docs/weidu-install.md).

## Never confuse these IDs

| Concept | Meaning | Example |
| --- | --- | --- |
| XML `<mod id>` / `<component modId>` | **Download folder** under the mods download dir only | `Tweaks-Anthology` |
| WeiDU mod id | Folder that contains the `.tp2` after staging (`stagedFolderName`) | `cdtweaks` |
| Component id `weiduFolder:N` | Designated WeiDU component **number** `N` | `stratagems:6020` |
| Component id without `:N` | WeiDU **LABEL**; resolve to `number` via `--list-components-json` | `cd_tweaks_adjust_evil_npc_reactions` → `4000` |

**Never** treat XML modId as the WeiDU mod id, as the `setup-*.exe` stem, or as a tp2 path segment.

## Install

1. Stage by XML modId (download folder) → discover tp2 → WeiDU id = tp2 parent folder.
2. List: configured `weidu.exe --nogame --noautoupdate --list-components-json <tp2> <lang>`.
3. Resolve labels to numbers from JSON `label[]` matching the component id (not XML display `label` / `name`).
4. Copy `weidu.exe` → `{gameDir}/setup-{weiduId}.exe` and run that exe (no tp2 argv) with `--noautoupdate`, `--safe-exit`, `--language`, `--use-lang`, `--force-install`, etc. Force-uninstall / rollback uses the same setup exe with `--force-uninstall` only (no `--safe-exit`).

## Resolution

- Prefer `:N` suffix → designated number.
- Else match WeiDU `label[]` to `componentId` (InstallSequence LABEL-as-id).
- Do not fall back to XML UI `label` / `name` for label-style ids.

## Reverse (WeiDU.log → XML)

Game-dir `WeiDU.log` (`~folder/tp2~ #lang #number`) maps back with the same rules:

- `weiduFolder:N` → match tp2 parent folder + number (no listing).
- LABEL ids → `--list-components-json` on the **already-installed** game-dir tp2, then invert `resolveComponentNumber` (numbered ids are not matched from another mod’s listing).
- Do not stage from the download dir when importing. Destination folders may already be modded; vanilla folders may not.
